{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1532950-new-homebrew-system-clauses-for-contracts","id":1532950,"title":"New Homebrew System - Clauses for Contracts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-03-21T12:01:22-07:00","id":1532950,"title":"New Homebrew System - Clauses for Contracts","content":"<i>Inspired by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> Clause Interpreter and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> Sincerest Flattery.</i><br /> <br /> So, I've been playing some Exalted: Essence and I was thinking of how they have a thing called Personal Modes - <i>&quot;A special rider on a Charm that suits the character\u2019s style of play. It should offer a meaningful bonus or inflict a dangerous penalty or do something unique that other modes the character has access to might not do.&quot;</i> I was thinking, what if this could be applied to CTL2e's Contracts?<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <u><b>Clauses</b></u> are unique benefits attached to Contracts similar to Seeming benefits that can be purchased with XP. However, they reflect the PC's playstyle and the Changeling's personality.<ul><li>Clauses cost the same as \u201cOut of Seeming Contract benefit.\u201d Due to their highly individualized nature, they cannot be learned through Pupil\u2019s Devotion.</li> <li>Clauses must still fit within the spirit of the Contract itself. The Changeling's Seeming, Kith, Court, Entitlement, Needle and Thread, and/or any combination thereof must be reflected as well.</li> <li>These benefits should be of a similar power level to a Seeming benefit of the Contract.</li> </ul><br /> Common Clauses alter:<ul><li>Adding an additional small way to fulfill the base loophole, or completely replacing the loophole. Choosing to replace the loophole renders the original loophole unusable.</li> <li>Adding an alternative Attribute OR Skill of the activation roll. Replacing both requires two separate Clauses.</li> <li>Adding a small benefit for free.</li> <li>Adding a larger benefit at the cost of additional glamour or a point of willpower.</li> </ul><br /> Examples:<ul><li>Dancing Daryl is a Moonborn Fairest who dances under the moonlight in elaborate performances with Boon of the Scuttling Spider. His player dislikes the inconvenience of having to both carry around and swallow a live spider when he wishes to magically go up walls in front of others. He works with the Storyteller to create a new loophole, and they come up with a new Clause: \u201cDancing Daryl\u2019s clever spider-like moves under the moon defy physics. The Loophole is replaced with: \u2018Be outdoors at night time.\u2019\u201d</li> <li>Mindless One is a Riddleseeker Wizened who likes using Murkblur mid-combat for a quick getaway, but wishes it had a longer term after-effect while still representing the \u201cmyriad distraction\u201d aspect. A new Clause is made: \u201cMindless One\u2019s image of Arcadia is so blank that it echoes within their target\u2019s mind. The target also suffers the Confused Condition.\u201d</li> <li>Brick Greenhammer is a Gremlin Ogre who likes crafting, unmaking, and busting things up with Touch of Wrath. However, she has a low Intelligence, usually favoring Strength when using Craft to forge new materials. A new Clause is made: \u201cBrick Greenhammer is much more direct with her wrath. Brick may use Strength instead of Intelligence to invoke this Contract.&quot;</li> </ul>---<br /> <br /> I do realize this would require a lot of collaboration between both player and storyteller, plus a good sense of game knowledge.<br /> <br /> Reactions, feedback and critique are welcome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-22T03:39:59-07:00","id":1532993,"title":"","content":"I don't think I would charge experience for a character to have a different loophole or Skill for a given contract. I would just let them have it, within the bounds of reason*.<br /> <br /> *Loopholes that are still appropriately thematic and not significantly easier to trip, Skills being replaced because the character isn't invested in the contract's written Skill but is invested in a Skill that is clearly also appropriate for the contract's effects and themes, and obviously not just going down the line and setting every power to use the same Skill so that a monofocus does everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}